{title: Come, Ye Sinners, Poor and Needy}
{artist: Joseph Hart / William Walker}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: Am}
{key_original: Gm}
{tempo: 112}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A]Come, ye sinners, poor [C]and nee[A7]dy,
[A7]Weak [C]and wounded, sick and [G]sore;
[C]Jesus rea[E]dy [Am]stands [G]to [C]save [Am]you,
[C]Full [Am]of pi[F]ty, [Am]love [E7]and pow[Am]er.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[A]I will arise and [C]go to [A7]Jesus,
[A7]He [C]will embrace me in [G]His [C]arms;
[C]In the [E]arms [Am]of [G]my [C]dear [Am]Sav[C]ior,
[Am]O there [F]are [Am]ten [E]thousand [Am]charms.
{end_of_chorus}
